WHAT PXA NETWORK ADDS

  * Pascal / SM60 (Tesla P100) support, which the upstream fork does not target:
    a torch-2.7.1 build variant, the PASCAL_SDPA and pascal_decode_attn backends,
    and the compat shims those require.
  * PXQ4 quantization - format, kernels, and the serving path for it.
  * A two-variant build (scripts/build-images.sh) so sm_60 and sm_70 each get the
    torch they actually need instead of one compromise build.

Renaming this distribution to pxa-vllm is a statement about WHOSE DISTRIBUTION
IT IS, not a claim over the upstream work. The attribution above travels with it.
